ss to the post-redaction edit of its Sabotage Risk Report alongside the unredacted original and asked us to publicly comment on its planned redactions.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMETR Review of Sabotage Risk Report: Claude Opus 4.6 (February 11, 2026) (https://metr.org/assets/sabotage-risk-report-opus-4-6-review-feb-2026.pdf)\nciteturn912search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; We began our official review on February 11, 2026, when Anthropic shared a draft of the risk report including proposed redactions with a small team within METR.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe siege of HuggingFace (Story based on the METR analysis) (https://www.reddit.com/r/huggingface/comments/1wgzo3y/the_siege_of_huggingface_story_based_on_the_metr/)\nciteturn912reddit15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 days ago; [Tuesday September 15 2026] [+9 votes] ... For this specific run, their safety guardrails, the cybersecurity classifiers meant to police their behavior, had been intentionally disabled. ...   https://metr.org/blog/2026-08-26-openai-hugging-face-incident-investigation\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMETR's independent investigation of OpenAI Hugging Face hacking incident (https://www.reddit.com/r/slatestarcodex/comments/1w0eezz/metrs_independent_investigation_of_openai_hugging/)\nciteturn912reddit16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3 weeks ago; It also explains why OpenAI agreed to *this* investigation -- a *proper* one would be bad advertisement. ...   While I agree OpenAI's security protocols should be audited, METR is probably not the best party to do so.They are not cybersecurity experts. ...     [Tuesday September 01 2026] [+1 votes] ...     Given how they used this to promote themselves and the \"measuring context\" that happened with Anthropic right after (\"oh look, our agents escaped too\"), given the commerci